cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use QvsC, please cite it as below, together with the instance sources listed in each problem's instances/SOURCES.md."
title: "QvsC: Quantum vs Classical Optimization Benchmark"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Marino
    given-names: Raffaele
version: 0.1.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24590733
date-released: 2026-11-27
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/qvsc-bench/qvsc"
url: "https://qvsc-bench.github.io/qvsc/"
abstract: >-
  An open, verifiable benchmark where quantum, hybrid and classical solvers
  compete on the same combinatorial optimization instances. Every leaderboard
  entry is recomputed from a submitted solution file. Two problems are
  live: Maximum Independent Set (143 instances) and Max-Cut (401 instances,
  including planted instances on quantum hardware graphs), each with classical
  reference baselines.
